 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law and the general business law, in\nrelation to requiring the display of a notice of responsibilities to protect\nunderground facilities",
    "basePrintNo": "S5509",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5509-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §119-b, Pub Serv L; amd §761, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5509\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law and the general business law, in\nrelation to requiring the display of a notice of responsibilities to\nprotect underground facilities\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would require entities that lease excavation equipment to\nprovide notice to lessees of equipment about their responsibility to\nprotect underground facilities.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 119-b of the public service law by adding a\nnew subdivision 9 requiring entities leasing excavation equipment to\nprovide lessees with notice of their responsibility to protect under-\nground facilities.\n\nSection two amends subdivision 2 of section 761 of the general business\nlaw by adding a new paragraph h stating that operators of underground\nfacilities provide entities that lease excavation equipment with the\ntelephone number of the system and a model notice to provide to equip-\nment lessees.\n\nSection three is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnderground facilities such as pipelines and wires have been damaged in\nthe past by users of excavation equipment. Though there are reminders\nfor users of such equipment to call before digging, these incidents\ncontinue to occur. This bill would require those leasing such equipment\nto provide users with notice of their responsibility to take steps to\nprotect underground facilities.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024- S9260- REFERRED TO ENERGY AND TELECOMMUNICATIONS\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall have become a law.\n",
